 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Pop them in the freezer for ten minutes, then pull them apart with your fingers. Then wash them in hot water while you turn on the tap and see if they pick up any dirt. That leaves a taste behind, so I only do that if I'm going to use them straight away. Otherwise, wash them in the shower. You can try using them for rough backgrounds, or mix them with fresh ones. Just paint over them though, they'll show through. Then throw them out and buy fresh ones. Loose bristles are dangerous, they can fly off and puncture skin.",
